From b834918eed34cd4120e510961bffb48df4f5316d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yahia <yahia.mostafa.elsayed@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:45:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 51/68] Expand packed 4:2:2 the way Metal samples it, so video
 is not black
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A `QuickTime Player` playback drew a solid black picture. The chain:
`bytes_per_pixel` had no answer for `0xf1`, so the ref-texture view refused
(`ref_texture_view_format_bpp`), so the fragment texture at index 3 did not
resolve, so the compositing draw was refused whole
(`draw_prepare_texture_resolve_missing stage=fragment index=3`). The frame was
never drawn at all.

`0xf1` is `MTLPixelFormatBGRG422`, and that is recovered rather than assumed:
the guest's own surface descriptor declares `bytes_per_row = 2560` at
`width = 1280` — two bytes a texel — and a `CVPixelFormatType` of `2vuy`,
`kCVPixelFormatType_422YpCbCr8`.

# Why not a Y'CbCr conversion

Vulkan can name this layout as `VK_FORMAT_B8G8R8G8_422_UNORM` and this host
supports `samplerYcbcrConversion`, but a Y'CbCr-converted combined image
sampler forbids the `ConstOffset` and `Offset` image operands. The guest's
fragment shader samples this texture 49 times, 11 of them with `ConstOffset` —
it is running a multi-tap scaling kernel. Binding it that way would make those
taps invalid, so the format is expanded at upload instead.

# What the expansion is, and is not

It moves no value through a colour transform. The guest's shader turns YCbCr
into colour, exactly as it does for the biplanar planes this device already
binds natively, so converting here would convert twice. What it undoes is the
subsampling — the part Metal's sampler does in hardware and an `R8G8` view
cannot.

The channel order is the format's own name. `BGRG422` is B, G, R, G across the
pair, and against `2vuy`'s Cb, Y0, Cr, Y1 that makes B the shared Cb, R the
shared Cr, and each G the pixel's own luma.

# Where it lives

Neither CPU rail. `texel_to_rgba8` takes one texel and a lone two-byte 4:2:2
texel cannot say which luma of its pair it carries, so the pair is the smallest
thing that converts — and `the_row_rail_and_the_texel_rail_answer_for_the_same_formats`
holds those two rails to one format set on purpose. `packed_422_expand_row` is
a third rail rather than an exception carved out of that one. An odd width is
refused: a trailing pixel has no pair to take chroma from.

Verified live on the x86/Vulkan rail against macOS 26: the film plays.
`ref_texture_view_format_bpp` 250 -> 0 and `draw_prepare_texture_resolve_missing`
-> 0, and the decoded bars read (254,32,0), (8,220,0), (255,242,0), (8,16,255),
(255,48,255) — saturated primaries in the right order, which is the check that
the chroma pair is not transposed, since a swapped Cb and Cr exchanges red and
blue.

